    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d368">

                <pb facs="0599" n="1185" sameAs="frus:frus1949v07p2/pg1185"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890.20/8–1249: Airgram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Taipei</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Macdonald</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Taipei</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-08-12">August 12,
                        1949</date>.<lb/>[Received August 24—5:18 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A–75. Assistant Military Attaché, Taipei, Captain Manning, told me that the
                    Generalissimo’s son made the remark to him and several other people that after
                    the Pacific Union is formed the Philippines and Korea will receive American
                    assistance after which China will be able to get aid through them.</p>
                <p>This apparently is the general line of Chinese thinking at present and was
                    expressed yesterday at an interview granted to Handleman of I. N. S. by K. C. Wu
                    who stated: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The release of the White Paper<anchor n="1" xml:id="d368-f1"/> by the
                            State Department exposes the unwise and impractical U.S. policy; but it
                            is hoped that the U.S. can extend indirect assistance to China through
                            the Pacific Union.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Macdonald</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
